The graph shows a company's share price at the beginning of each month.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[{"name":"shareSeries","hex":"268CFF","reason":"One share-price time series and its sampled price markers"}],"reference":"Investments and Loans 1_Investment, Dividends Q8(a), lines 1647-1654 adaptation"}
\definecolor{shareSeries}{HTML}{268CFF}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.2cm,y=1cm]
\draw[black!15,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=0.5] (0,0) grid (3,3);
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(3.5,0) node[below right] {Month};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,3.5) node[above left] {Price (\$)};
\foreach \x/\m in {1/Apr,2/May,3/Jun} \node[below] at (\x,0) {\m};
\foreach \y/\v in {0/8.00,0.5/8.50,1/9.00,1.5/9.50,2/10.00,2.5/10.50,3/11.00} \node[left] at (0,\y) {\v};
\draw[very thick,shareSeries] (1,2.5)--(2,1.5)--(3,2);
\foreach \pt in {(1,2.5),(2,1.5),(3,2)} \fill[shareSeries] \pt circle (2pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What was the share price at the beginning of May?
